# TALLOW — a man the machine keeps fat, and burns.
# Owner brief (2026-11-14): "a corpulent mass of waddling flesh inspired by
# Cronenberg, Eraserhead, Giger, Garage: Bad Dream Adventure", with two
# reference images of a fat arm-cannon demon as the point of departure (the
# imp's lesson: a reference is where the design starts, not what it copies).
#
# THE IDEA. A rendering vat that walks. He was a man; the machine renders his
# own fat in a boiler sunk into his back and pumps it down to the cannons his
# forearms have GROWN into. He fires burning tallow. He is the fuel tank.
#
# THE DIRECTION (owner, 2026-11-14, second pass): Cronenberg fusion. The
# machinery is not bolted on; the meat has swallowed it (the Videodrome
# gun-hand). The forearm flesh runs on over each cannon's breech, the boiler
# is sunk in a swollen rim of back fat, the hoses dive under the skin. The
# first pass's burners and belly siphons read as "silly" and are gone; the
# face is his own, not the zombie's. Third pass: the cannons heavy and
# industrial (the second pass's were "too floral"), blood at every place the
# metal goes into him, and the breathing mask back on his face.
#
# AUTHORED FROM THE BRIEF. No reference mesh or plate, so blob:measure and
# blob:rings exit 2; every number is a design decision with its reason beside
# it, checked on the CPU field (scripts/tmp/venus-sections.ts tallow).
#
# THE SPLIT (biomech-style.md): flesh is prims, few and LARGE; fat rolls,
# stretch marks, cellulite and veins are the baked body normal map
# (tallow.detail, not baked yet); the cannons, the boiler and the hoses are
# sculpted kit mesh (assets-source/tallow-kit/).
#
# THE THREE BEATS, in order of distance:
#   1. THE MASS. Wider than a doorway is tall-ish: 1.3 m across the gut on a
#      1.9 m body, the belly an apron hanging to the knees, legs two short
#      pillars under it. No yaw shows a waist.
#   2. THE ARMS. Held out and forward by the fat under them, each forearm a
#      sleeve of meat that a bone-metal cannon (kit) grows out of. Two big
#      dark bores with fire in them, pointed at the player.
#   3. THE HEAD. Broad and bald, sunk between the shoulder mounds in a
#      collar of jowl, with a mean face low on it: a V brow over red ember
#      eyes in slanted sockets, a hooked nose, and a heavy breathing mask
#      strapped into the flesh over his mouth, hoses down into his chest.
model tallow
  # Crown at ~1.89 since the legs were cut down (owner, fifth look: "doesnt
  # quite read as corpulent ... maybe his legs should be shorter"): barely
  # taller than the venus (1.79) and a third wider than he is deep.
  # His size is WIDTH; a 2.3 m body would need the legs lengthened and he
  # would stop reading as a waddler.
  height 1.89
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Hip line 0.72 (root 0.62 + 0.10). STUMPS: legs 0.30 + 0.24 below it land
  # the ankle at 0.18, inside an iron boot (kit, make_boots.py) whose sole is
  # the floor. Legs 29% of his height (they were 39%, and a man's are 50%): at
  # 39% he stood like a big man, not a mass of fat on stumps (owner).
  #
  # EVERY ABSOLUTE HEIGHT IN THE COMMENTS BELOW the hips (y 1.36, 1.875, ...)
  # was measured before this cut: subtract 0.16 (LOWER in
  # scripts/tallow-surface.ts, which the kit and the skin generator read).
  root pelvis at 0.62 len=0.10

  # The venus's heavy posture, more of it: the lumbar sways BACK (pitch -6)
  # to counterweight the gut, the chest comes forward over it and the head
  # hangs forward of the shoulders. Positive pitch is forward (+z).
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=-6 len=0.28
  # 12, not 8 (owner, 2026-11-14: arms "more ape gorilla like"): the shoulders
  # roll forward over the gut, a gorilla's hunch.
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=12 len=0.30
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=6  len=0.12
  # A short neck (0.10) buried in the jowl collar: the head sits IN the
  # shoulders, but the whole face clears them (at 0.04 the collar covered it
  # to the nose on the CPU silhouette).
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=16 len=0.12
  # 0.30: the face block centres the head 0.55 along it (y ~1.86).
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=6  len=0.30

  mirror
    # Sockets at x ~0.46: the shoulders are as wide as the gut's flanks, so
    # the arms start outside the chest mass (0.42 half-width up there).
    bone clavicle parent=spine2  side=0.040 dir=side len=0.42
    # GORILLA ARMS (owner, 2026-11-14: "his arms should be longer, more ape
    # gorilla like"): the upper arm 0.50 (was 0.36) and the forearm 0.44 (was
    # 0.40), and they hang LOW and AHEAD of him (upper arm pitch 14, forearm
    # 45; at 6 / 62 the muzzles hung at hip height, y 0.90): the muzzles at
    # y ~0.70, a hand's breadth over the knees. Pushed OUT by the mass (tilt
    # 42: the elbow at x ~0.80 clears a gut 0.63 in half-width). They point
    # down and forward at rest; the brace (attack.ts) raises them level to
    # fire. The venus's rule (arms on a wide body cannot hang) taken to its
    # end.
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=42 pitch=14  len=0.50
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=10 pitch=45  len=0.44
    # 0.246: the barrel's last length; the tail (handTip) is the muzzle, forearm
    # t 1.56 along the cannon (make_cannons.py T_MUZZLE x 0.44 = 0.686 m from
    # the elbow, and 0.44 + 0.246 = 0.686).
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down tilt=10 pitch=48  len=0.246
    # Legs set WIDE (side 0.23) and splayed a little (tilt 4): thighs 0.40 m
    # thick cannot stand under the hips, and the wide base rocks side to
    # side as he walks.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down tilt=4 side=0.23  len=0.30
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=-2           len=0.24
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                    len=0.22
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — the mass. Big prims, wide blends (0.05-0.06: a blend that suits
  # a man's torso is a crease on a body this size).
  # ============================================================
  # PELVIS / HIPS — the base the gut hangs from, half-width 0.50.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.60 r=0.300 wide=1.66 tall=0.80 deep=1.05 blend=0.060 core
  # THE REAR — two heavy mounds low behind the hips, so the profile has a
  # shelf at the back to answer the gut at the front (without it the side
  # view is an egg on legs).
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.10 offset=(0.170,-0.020,-0.200) r=0.240 tall=0.95 blend=0.050 both
  # THE GUT — the biggest thing on him. Centre y ~1.02, forward of the spine
  # (z 0.20), half-width 0.63, front reach z ~0.64. tall 0.92 keeps it a
  # sagging mass rather than a ball.
  blob torso on spine1 at=0.35 offset=(0,-0.030,0.200) r=0.440 wide=1.44 tall=0.92 deep=1.00 blend=0.060
  # THE APRON — the gut's lower lip, hanging forward of the thighs to y ~0.32,
  # below the knees (0.42): from the front you see belly over two short
  # pillars of shin and boot. This overhang is what says "fat" rather than
  # "big": the venus's apron, more than doubled.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(0,-0.100,0.330) r=0.260 wide=1.80 tall=0.78 deep=0.95 blend=0.055
  # FLANK ROLLS — love handles standing off the waist over the hip, so the
  # front outline steps out and in instead of running as one smooth barrel.
  blob torso on spine1 at=0.05 offset=(0.470,0.000,-0.020) r=0.200 tall=0.62 deep=1.25 blend=0.045 both
  # RIBCAGE / BACK — narrower than the gut (half-width 0.44): the body is a
  # pear, widest at the belly. A broad slab of back fat behind it.
  bar  torso on chest  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.300 r2=0.280 wide=1.46 deep=0.98 blend=0.060
  blob torso on chest  at=0.55 offset=(0,0,-0.150) r=0.260 wide=1.55 tall=1.05 deep=0.75 blend=0.055
  # BREASTS — heavy, sagging onto the top of the gut (tip= hangs down and
  # forward), wide-set so a cleft runs down the sternum into the belly.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.55 offset=(0.200,0.000,0.250) tip=(0.030,-0.130,0.060) r=0.190 r2=0.160 wide=1.10 deep=0.90 blend=0.040 both
  # THE YOKE — a hump of fat across the shoulders and the back of the neck,
  # HIGHER than the chin: the head sits in a nest, never on a column.
  # r 0.165: at 0.25 its top (y 1.83) buried the whole head (first render).
  bar  torso on spine2 from=0.00 to=0.80 r=0.165 r2=0.140 wide=2.30 deep=1.25 offset=(0,-0.020,-0.040) blend=0.055
  blob torso on spine2 at=1.00 offset=(0,0.020,-0.170) r=0.170 wide=1.60 tall=0.80 blend=0.050
  # JOWL COLLAR — a roll of fat round the front of the neck, under the chin
  # (the head's own prims blend down into it).
  blob torso on spine2 at=1.00 offset=(0,-0.030,0.100) r=0.120 wide=1.60 tall=0.65 deep=0.90 blend=0.040
  # THE BOILER'S RIM (Cronenberg: the meat has grown round the metal). The
  # boiler (kit, make_back.py) is sunk into his back at y 1.36 with its
  # centre only 4.5 cm off the skin; this swollen roll of fat rises round its
  # edge (half-width 0.235, half-height 0.215), seated on the PROBED back
  # skin (surface.json: z -0.32 to -0.35 round it) about a centimetre out,
  # so the sac reads as sunk into a wound rather than strapped on. All from
  # the chest at y 1.36 (at=0.678). Unpainted: painted raw they read as red
  # stripes down his back (first look).
  blob torso on chest at=0.678 offset=(0.225,0.000,-0.335) r=0.070 tall=2.40 deep=0.80 blend=0.035 both
  blob torso on chest at=0.678 offset=(0.150,0.170,-0.326) r=0.064 wide=1.40 deep=0.80 blend=0.035 both
  blob torso on chest at=0.678 offset=(0.000,0.215,-0.342) r=0.070 wide=2.00 deep=0.80 blend=0.035
  blob torso on chest at=0.678 offset=(0.150,-0.170,-0.348) r=0.064 wide=1.40 deep=0.80 blend=0.035 both
  blob torso on chest at=0.678 offset=(0.000,-0.210,-0.356) r=0.070 wide=2.00 deep=0.80 blend=0.035

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — shoulder mounds, upper arms like hams, and a forearm SLEEVE: the
  # flesh runs on down the forearm and swallows the cannon's breech (kit,
  # make_cannons.py); its breech block goes into a fat lip at t 0.62, torn
  # and bloody where the metal meets the meat (kit gore). The hand bone
  # is the barrel's last length, and its tail is the muzzle.
  # ============================================================
  # Shoulder mound, blended wide (the zombie's shoulder lesson: one mound in
  # every pose, never a ball on a stick).
  # Gorilla-heavy: a bigger shoulder mound and a thicker, longer upper arm.
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 offset=(0,-0.040,0) r=0.225 tall=0.85 blend=0.050 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.05 to=0.98 r=0.185 r2=0.150 blend=0.040 mirror
  # The hanging mass under and behind the upper arm.
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.42 offset=(0,-0.020,-0.055) r=0.150 tall=1.80 blend=0.040 mirror
  # Elbow, and the sleeve SWELLING toward the breech (0.140 -> 0.150): the
  # meat bulges where the metal is inside it. A bar's rounded END CAP reaches
  # its radius past `to=` (0.150 is 0.34 of the 0.44 m forearm), so a sleeve
  # authored to 0.56 really ran on to t ~0.93 and hid the cannon's chamber:
  # it stops at 0.40 and its cap ends the meat at t ~0.78.
  blob arm on forearm  at=0.00 r=0.142 blend=0.030 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.00 to=0.40 r=0.140 r2=0.150 blend=0.025 mirror
  # A tumorous swelling on the top-outer side of the sleeve: the growth is
  # uneven, never a clean tube.
  blob arm on forearm  at=0.30 offset=(0.055,0.070,0.010) r=0.085 blend=0.030 mirror
  # THE LIP the cannon's breech block goes into (make_cannons.py: an
  # octagon of r 0.152 from forearm t 0.62): fat, r 0.160 -> 0.150, so at the
  # block's back face the flesh is r ~0.145 and rolls right up against it;
  # its end cap (to t ~0.90) is hidden inside the block. Unpainted: the blood
  # where metal meets meat is kit (`gore`, torn lumps and drips), because a
  # painted band read as a red sweatband (second look).
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.38 to=0.52 r=0.160 r2=0.150 blend=0.012 mirror
  # (No tendons along the barrel: on the industrial cannon they read as pink
  # sausages stuck on the machine. The meat stops at the breech block; the
  # blood there is kit.)
  # CORE inside the cannon (kit): the forearm rod and a stub of hand, all
  # behind the throat plug (make_cannons.py: t 1.38 of the forearm), so
  # none of it shows down the bore.
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.35 to=1.00 r=0.050 blend=0.006 mirror color=2a2c30 metal gloss=0.5
  bar  arm on hand     from=0.00 to=0.10 r=0.045 blend=0.006 mirror color=2a2c30 metal gloss=0.5

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — two short pillars: thighs 0.40 m thick (and mostly under the
  # apron) tapering to a knee as thick as a man's thigh, elephant shins, and
  # the feet crammed into iron boots (kit) with the ankle fat spilling over
  # the cuffs.
  # ============================================================
  # Root ball seated a little down the thigh (the venus's rule: at the hip
  # joint it reaches up and fills in the crotch).
  blob leg on thigh at=0.12 r=0.205 deep=1.08 blend=0.045 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.05 to=1.00 r=0.205 r2=0.150 wide=0.96 deep=1.06 blend=0.040 mirror
  # Knee: a fold of fat hanging over it at the front.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.00 offset=(0,0.010,0.030) r=0.165 blend=0.030 mirror
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.00 to=0.95 r=0.150 r2=0.135 blend=0.025 mirror
  # THE FAT OVER THE BOOT: a roll squeezed up out of the cuff (make_boots.py:
  # cuff top y 0.28, radius 0.175 round the ankle), bulging past it to r ~0.19
  # at y ~0.30. Fat crammed into gear is the corpulence read.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.55 r=0.190 tall=0.55 blend=0.030 mirror
  # Foot: a CORE inside the boot (it shows nowhere), heel to toe.
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.070 r2=0.060 tip=(0.010,0,0.200) wide=1.30 tall=0.80 blend=0.020 offset=(0,-0.080,-0.050) mirror

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD — HIS OWN (owner, 2026-11-14: "a new face rather than reuse the
  # zombie one ... evil and ugly", the ogre as a reference for the nose and
  # ears). The ogre's road: every feature is a prim, the face block is a nub
  # and a generated decal draws only the mouth's cavity and teeth
  # (scripts/make-tallow-face.py). Skull bone: (0, 1.690, 0.058) ->
  # (0, 1.989, 0.090), len 0.30, nearly upright, so skull t = (y - 1.690) /
  # 0.298 and the axis sits at z ~0.06-0.08.
  # ============================================================
  # Neck: r 0.13, under the cranium's 0.155 so the cranium stays the
  # FATTEST head prim (the decal's head-space frame).
  bar  head on neck from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.130 wide=1.30 blend=0.030
  # CRANIUM — bald, broad and LOW: wider than tall. Centre y 1.875, z 0.079;
  # semi-axes 0.174 x 0.167 x 0.167, front at z ~0.245. A tall dome (tall
  # 1.22) read as a goofy baby head (owner: "too goofy ... more evil and
  # mean"); a low brutal crown sits the scowl under it. It must stay the head
  # prim with the biggest r x max scale (0.174), because the mouth decal
  # projects from that prim (lab-main.ts headShape): on an earlier look the
  # jaw beat it and the teeth landed under the lower lip.
  blob head on skull at=0.62 r=0.155 wide=1.12 tall=1.08 deep=1.08 blend=0.014
  # JAW MASS — wider than the cranium and slung low and forward: the face
  # sits LOW on the head, the mancubus's read. Centre y 1.745, z 0.126,
  # front z ~0.26; half-width 0.165 (r x max scale 0.165, under the cranium's).
  blob head on skull at=0.25 offset=(0,-0.020,0.060) r=0.125 wide=1.32 tall=0.88 deep=1.08 blend=0.014
  # Jowls hanging past the jaw line into the collar.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.120,-0.030,0.050) r=0.105 tall=1.30 blend=0.030 both
  # Double chin.
  blob head on skull at=0.20 offset=(0,-0.040,0.100) r=0.105 wide=1.60 tall=0.72 blend=0.030
  # Nape roll: the back of the skull runs into the yoke.
  blob head on skull at=0.35 offset=(0,-0.010,-0.130) r=0.125 wide=1.35 tall=0.80 blend=0.035
  # THE SCOWL (owner, 2026-11-14: "more evil and mean and have red eyes").
  # The first face read as goofy: a straight brow over sleepy slits with
  # bags, a round bulb nose and a soft mouth. Mean is ANGLES: a V brow, eyes
  # slanting up and out in sunken sockets, heavy cheekbones, a hooked nose,
  # tusks, and a mouth whose corners turn down. Cranium surface for placing:
  # z = 0.079 + 0.167 sqrt(1 - (x/0.174)^2 - ((y - 1.875)/0.167)^2); skull t
  # = (y - 1.690) / 0.298, and the bone's own z at t is 0.058 + 0.031 t.
  #
  # BROWS — two bars in a V, the inner ends LOW and knotted together over the
  # nose (y 1.881, z 0.256), the outer ends high (y 1.907) and overhanging
  # the temples by ~3 cm. Chamfered, so the underside is a crease the
  # sockets sit in. (Brows that meet as one level bar read as a hat brim:
  # the imp's lesson; this one breaks at the knot.)
  bar  head on skull from=0.66 to=0.66 r=0.030 tall=0.80 blend=0.006 chamfer offset=(0.012,-0.006,0.178) tip=(0.093,0.026,-0.016) both
  # The knot between them: a frowning bulge over the bridge of the nose.
  blob head on skull at=0.61 offset=(0,0,0.168) r=0.022 wide=0.90 tall=1.40 blend=0.008
  # SOCKETS — slanted dark pits under the brows, inner end low, outer end
  # high, sunk ~4 mm under the skin. Painted near-black so the red reads.
  bar  head on skull from=0.57 to=0.57 r=0.014 blend=0.004 offset=(0.024,-0.004,0.162) tip=(0.050,0.012,-0.014) both color=2a0e0c gloss=0.3
  # EYES — small hot RED embers in the sockets (the ogre's 0.9 glow: the one
  # lit thing on his face under the brow's shadow).
  blob head on skull at=0.577 offset=(0.048,-0.002,0.163) r=0.010 blend=0.002 both color=ff1a0a gloss=0.8 glow=0.9
  # CHEEKBONES — heavy ridges raking up and out under the eyes: the sneer.
  bar  head on skull from=0.48 to=0.48 r=0.020 blend=0.008 offset=(0.030,-0.004,0.158) tip=(0.070,0.018,-0.026) both
  # NOSE — broad and hooked, not a bulb (the bulb read as a clown's): a bridge
  # out of the brow knot down to a squashed tip with flared wings.
  bar  head on skull from=0.56 to=0.56 r=0.022 blend=0.008 offset=(0,0,0.165) tip=(0,-0.045,0.040)
  blob head on skull at=0.40 offset=(0,0.000,0.185) r=0.030 wide=1.50 tall=0.80 deep=0.85 blend=0.008
  blob head on skull at=0.40 offset=(0.032,-0.004,0.170) r=0.018 tall=0.85 blend=0.006 both
  # EARS — small, low, backswept points (the ogre's, scaled up), crumpled by
  # a lump at the root.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 r=0.036 r2=0.005 wide=0.55 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(0.150,-0.010,-0.010) tip=(0.040,0.050,-0.065) both
  blob head on skull at=0.52 offset=(0.152,-0.020,-0.005) r=0.026 blend=0.008 both
  # LIPS — thick, parted, unpainted (painted glossy red they read as clown
  # lips): one BENT bar each, corner to corner, ~5 mm proud of the jaw. Both
  # bow UP in the middle, so the corners turn DOWN: a grimace, not a smile.
  # The gap between them is where the decal's dark cavity and teeth show.
  bar  head on skull from=0.22 to=0.22 r=0.016 tall=0.95 blend=0.005 offset=(-0.080,0.000,0.190) tip=(0.160,0,0) bend=(0,0.018,0.050)
  bar  head on skull from=0.02 to=0.02 r=0.020 tall=0.90 blend=0.005 offset=(-0.078,0.000,0.186) tip=(0.156,0,0) bend=(0,0.012,0.050)
  # (No tusks: the breathing mask's plate covers the mouth, and they came
  # out through it. The lips and the mouth decal stay under it for when the
  # mask is shot off.)

# THE FACE ROAD (the ogre's): no mesh, so no bake. All structure is prims
# above; headRadius ~0 turns off the generated ellipsoid so it cannot fight
# the authored cranium.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.008

# A generated MOUTH decal at MULTIPLY (scripts/make-tallow-face.py): a wide
# drooping grimace, a dark wet cavity and ragged teeth. The eyes are prims, so
# the sheet's own glow is gated off.
#
# hs is relative to the cranium (centre y 1.875, semi 0.174 x 0.167). The
# mouth sits between the lips at y ~1.727: hs.y = -0.148 / 0.167 = -0.886.
# Scale 0.388: the drawing's half-width (0.19 of the sheet) is then
# 0.19 x 0.174 / 0.388 = 0.085 m, the lips' half-width. Drawing centred at
# uv 0.5, so centre = 0.5 + 0.886 x 0.388 = 0.844.
sheet
  image       tallow-face.png
  decal       0
  projScaleX  0.388
  projScaleY  0.388
  projCentreX 0.50
  projCentreY 0.844
  eyeGlowCut  0.99
  eyeGlowAmp  0

# Interior bones for wound reveals: the limb bones auto-derive. A low ratio
# (0.22): the bones of a man inside a body three times his girth.
bones
  ratio 0.22
  blob head on skull at=0.62 r=0.120 wide=0.98 tall=1.10 deep=1.06

# ============================================================
# PALETTE — tallow: pale, waxy, sweating candle fat with a jaundiced cast
# and bruise-purple mottle; wetter and glossier than the zombie. Eyeballed;
# the frames judge it.
# ============================================================
palette
  baseColor     0.60 0.47 0.38
  deepColor     0.50 0.08 0.07
  charColor     0.14 0.09 0.08
  specIntensity 0.60
  specRoughness 0.34
  fresnelBoost  0.80
  translucency  0.34
  wetness       0.60
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.05
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.012
  mottleAmp     0.32
  mottleScale   1.4
  mottleColor   0.34 0.22 0.30
  grain         0.12
